      "content": "There is no scientific evidence that high-energy particle exposure can enable humans to perceive quantum fluctuations or predict future events through peripheral vision. Current neuroscience and physics confirm that the human brain and retinas operate only on macroscopic scales, unable to detect single quantum events or process probability densities to foresee accidents. While the event is undoubtedly stressful and had a significant psychological impact, there are no known theories linking Fermilab radiation exposure to this specific visual predictive phenomenon. It is highly advisable to seek evaluation from a neurologist or psychiatrist to understand if these symptoms are related to stress-induced synesthesia or another physiological condition.",
